ll,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2025-10-24T08:12:16Z","updated_at":"2025-10-24T12:23:37Z","closed_at":"2025-10-24T12:21:28Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.4.1 and 4.5.1\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 10 - Godot Engine v4.5.1.stable.mono.official.f62fdbde1 - https://godotengine.org Vulkan 1.4.312 - Forward+ - Using Device #0: NVIDIA - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3070 Ti\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen playing textures in AnimatedSprite2D， sometimes horizontal lines flicker. My pixel map base size is 48x48. As shown in the figure\n\n<img width=\"341\" height=\"309\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/19686770-fb82-4f3a-91d5-003795d8095e\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nWhen playing animations with AnimatedSprite2D, when moving characters or objects, such as cows, in the tilemapplayer, this happens when the Y coordinate of the tilemapLayer is less than 0. The object's YSortnabled = true. This phenomenon does not occur when the Y coordinate of the tilemapLayer is greater than 0.\n<img width=\"2549\" height=\"1264\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bd60bf37-c069-475e-8699-a5e346ee3d18\" />\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[A_FOLKS_TALE.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23115458/A_FOLKS_TALE.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"bytt67","id":35530352,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NTMwMzUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35530352?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bytt67","html_url":"https://github.com/bytt67","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bytt67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.co